  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp;The given reactions are:<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow/><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow/><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>He</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mn>3</mn><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>He</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math></p><p>Mass defect<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>014</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>001</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>007</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>008</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>amu</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>026</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>amu</mi></math><br /><br />Energy released<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>026</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>931</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>026</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>931</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>87</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math><br /><br />This is the energy produced by the consumption of three deuteron atoms.<br /><br />Therefore Total energy released by 10<sup>40</sup> deuterons<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>87</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1028</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math><br /><br />The average power radiated is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>16</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>16</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. Therefore, the total time to exhaust all deuterons of the star, time taken will be<br /><br /><math><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mn>1.29</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>28</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>16</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1.29</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn></mn><mn></mn></mrow></math><math><mrow><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>&#160;&#8776;&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>12</mn></msup></mrow></math></p>"
  }
